// Per-species balance numbers for every creature body kind.
//
// This file is the ONLY source of these four numbers. The struct behind each
// body kind below has one required field per species, so leaving a species out
// is a hard deserialisation error naming the missing field at start-up -- it
// cannot silently inherit somebody else's number, which is exactly what the
// `_ =>` arms this file replaced used to do.
//
//   mass         kilograms. Feeds physics: buoyancy, drag, swim/fly thrust and
//                knockback. Values marked `~` + a check mark were sanity-checked
//                against the real-world animal; discrepancies between our model
//                size and the real animal have not necessarily been accounted
//                for.
//   base_health  hit points before any scaling. Roughly tracks the threat tier
//                in `Body::threat_tier` (which is still code -- it is a
//                taxonomy, read per tick, and the compiler checks it
//                exhaustively).
//   base_poise   the stagger pool. 100 is the standard creature value.
//   base_energy  the stamina/ability pool. 100 is the standard creature value.
//
// Edits hot-reload, but every one of these numbers is snapshotted into a
// component when an entity spawns, so a change only reaches creatures that
// spawn after it -- respawn or re-enter the chunk to see it.
//
// Body kinds NOT here, and where their numbers live instead:
//   Humanoid  derived from the body scaler (`common/src/comp/body/mod.rs`)
//   Object    per-object arms in `mod.rs` -- props/projectiles, not creatures
//   Item      flat, in `mod.rs`
//   Ship      `common/src/comp/body/ship.rs`
//   Plugin    `assets/common/plugin_bodies.ron`
(
